hadiths[61]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1808","On the authority of Al-Nawwas bin Samaan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned the Antichrist one morning, so he lowered it and raised it until we thought he was in a group of palm trees. When we went to him, he recognized that about us, and he said: “What is the matter with you?” We said: O Messenger of Allah, I mentioned the Antichrist in the morning, so I lowered it until we thought he was in a group of palm trees, and he said: 'What I fear most for you is other than the Dajjal.' The Antichrist is the most fearful of you. If he emerges while I am among you, then I will be his defender/protector over you. And if he emerges while I am not among you, then a man is a pilgrim on his own behalf, and Allah is my successor over every Muslim. He is a young man with curly hair. It is as if I liken him to Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan. Whoever of you meets him should recite to him the opening verses of Surat al-Kahf. He will emerge from a narrow pass between the Levant (Syria) and Iraq, he will spread corruption to the right and to the left. O servants of Allah, so stand firm. We said: O Messenger. Allah and what did he remain on earth? He said: “Forty days: a day like a year, a day like a month, a day like a week, and the rest of his days are like your days.” We said: O Messenger of Allah, is that day that is like a year sufficient for us to pray a day? He said: No, estimate his destiny for him. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, what is his speed on earth? He said: “Like rain driven by the wind, it comes upon the people, and they call upon them, and they believe in it, and they respond to it. So it commands the sky and it rains, and the earth and it sprouts, their livestock will return to them in the evening, with the longest of humps, the fullest of udders, and the longest of flanks. Then the people come and call upon them, and they respond to His saying, and He turns away from them, and they become barren, with nothing of their money in their hands. He passes by ruins, and he says to her: Bring out your treasures, and their treasures will follow him like the dragonflies of bees. Then he calls a man full of youth and strikes him with a sword, cutting him into two pieces as easily as shooting an arrow at its target. Then he calls him, and he accepts, and his face beams with laughter. While he was like that, Allah Almighty sent the Messiah, the son of Mary (ﷺ) and he descended at the white minaret east of Damascus between two dyed garments, placing his palms on the wings of two angels. When he lowered his head, he dripped, and when he raised it, he descended. Mountains like pearls flow from it, and it is not permissible for an infidel to find himself without dying, and his soul will end up wherever his gaze ends, so he pursues it until he overtakes him at the door of Lydda and kills him. Then Jesus (ﷺ) comes, a people whom Allah has protected from him, and he wipes their faces and tells them of their ranks in Paradise. While this is the case, Allah Almighty revealed to Jesus (ﷺ) “Indeed, I have brought out My servants, whom no one has the power to fight.” So my servants marched to the Mount, and Allah sent Gog and Magog, and they would descend from every direction. The first of them would pass by Lake Tiberias and drink what was in it, and the last of them would pass by and say: This time there was water, and the Prophet of Allah, Jesus (ﷺ) was besieged. And his companions, until the head of a bull for one of them is better than a hundred dinars for one of you today. Then the Prophet of Allah Jesus (ﷺ) and his companions, may Allah be pleased with them, wish to go to Allah Almighty, so Allah Almighty sends migraines upon them. Then the Prophet of Allah Jesus (ﷺ) and his companions, may Allah be pleased with them, descend to the earth, and they do not find a place of an inch on the ground that is not filled with their saliva and stench. Then the Prophet of Allah Jesus (ﷺ) and his companions, may Allah be pleased with them, desire to Allah Almighty, so Allah Almighty sends a bird like the necks of a camel, which carries them and throws them wherever Allah wills, then Allah Almighty sends rain from which there will not be a house of mud or wool, and it washes the earth until it leaves it slippery. Then it is said to the earth: Grow your fruit, and increase your blessing. On that day, the group will eat from the pomegranate, and they will take shade from its shell. He will bless [the production of] milk until the milk of a single lactating camel will suffice a group of people, the milk of a single lactating cow will suffice a tribe of people, and the milk of a single lactating sheep will suffice a clan of people. So while they Likewise, when Allah Almighty sent a pleasant wind, it took them under their armpits, capturing the soul of every believer and every Muslim. And the worst of people will remain being tossed around in it like donkeys, for upon them the Hour will come.” [Muslim] “And dragonflies”: male bees. “And two wings”: meaning two pieces. “And the target”: the target at which the crossbow is aimed, i.e.: he throws it with a shot like a crossbow to the target. “And the abandoned” with the neglected and lexicalized signifier, which is: the dyed garment. His saying: “He will not be judged” means there is no power. “Walnaf”: worm. “And my horse”: the plural of “faris”, meaning the dead man. And “al-Zalqa”: with the opening of the za’i and the lam and with the qaf,... It was narrated: the zalfa with the dhammah of the za’i and the sakah of the lam with the fa’, which is the mirror. ... “and the gang”: the group. “And the messengers” with a kasra on the r: milk. “The vaccinia” means the milk. “Al-Fa’am” with a kasra on the fa’ followed by an extended hamza: the group. ... “and the thigh” of the people: without the tribe."
"1809","On the authority of Rabi’ bin Harash, he said: I went with Abu Masoud Al-Ansari to Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, may Allah be pleased with them, and Abu Masoud said to him, “Tell me what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the Antichrist. He said: “The Antichrist will emerge, and he has water and fire with him. As for what people see as water, it will burn, and as for what people see as fire, it is cold, fresh water. Whoever of you catches it, let him fall into what he sees as fire, for it is fresh, good water.” Abu Masoud said: And I heard it. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1810","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Dajjal (the Antichrist) will appear in my Ummah and he will stay in the world for forty. I do not know whether this will be forty days or forty months or forty years. Allah will then send (Prophet) 'Isa (Jesus)"," son of Maryam (Mary). 'Isa will pursue him and slaughter him. Then people will survive for seven years (i.e."," after the demise of 'Isa) in the state that there will be no rancour between two persons. Then Allah will send a cool breeze from the side of Ash-Sham. None will remain upon the face of the earth having the smallest particle of good or Faith in him but he will die"," so much so that even if someone amongst you will enter the innermost part of a mountain"," this breeze will reach that place also and will cause him to die. Only the wicked people will survive and they will be as fast as birds (i.e."," to commit evil) and as ferocious towards one another as wild beasts. They will never appreciate the good"," nor condemn evil. Then Shaitan (Satan) will come to them in the garb of a man and will say: 'Will you not obey me?' They will say: 'What do you order us to do?' He will command them to worship idols. They will have abundance of sustenance and will lead comfortable lives. Then the Trumpet will be blown. Every one hearing it"," will turn his neck towards it and will raise it. The first one to hear that Trumpet will be a man who will be busy repairing the basin for his camels. He will become unconscious. Allah will send"," or will cause to send"," rain which will be like dew and there will grow out of it (like wild growth) the bodies of the people. Then the second Trumpet will be blown and they will stand up and begin to look around. Then it will be said: 'O people! Go to your Rubb.' Then there will be a command: 'Make them stand there.' After it they will be called to account. Then it will be said: 'Separate from them the share of the Fire.' It will be asked: 'How much?' It will be said: 'Nine hundred and ninety-nine out of every thousand.' That will be the Day which will make children hoary-headed men because of its terror and that will be the Day when the Shin will be uncovered.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"1811","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \There will be no land which will not be trampled by Dajjal (the Antichrist) but Makkah and Al-Madinah; and there will be no passage leading to them which will not be guarded by the angels"," arranged in rows. Dajjal will appear in a barren place adjacent to Al- Madinah and the city will be shaken three times. Allah will expel from it every disbeliever and hypocrite.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"1812","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Dajjal (the Antichrist) will be followed by seventy thousand Jews of Isfahan wearing long robes.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"1813","On the authority of Umm Sharik, may Allah be pleased with her, that she heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying: “The people will flee from the Antichrist to the mountains” [Muslim]."
"1814","On the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “There is no affair greater than the Antichrist between the creation of Adam and the arrival of the Hour.” [Muslim]."
"1815","I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, \Dajjal (the Antichrist) will come forth and a person from amongst the believers will go towards him and the armed watchmen of Dajjal will meet him and they will say to him: 'Where do you intend to go?' He will say: 'I intend to go to this one who has appeared.' They will say to him: 'Don't you believe in our lord (meaning Dajjal)?' He will say: 'There (i.e."," we know Him to be Allah"," Alone"," without any partners) is nothing hidden about our Rubb.' Some of them will say: 'Let us kill him'"," but some others will say: 'Has your lord (Dajjal) not forbidden you to kill anyone without his consent?' So they will take him to Dajjal. When the believer will see him"," he will say: 'O people! This is Dajjal about whom the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has informed us.' Dajjal will have him laid on his stomach and have his head. He will be struck on his back and on his stomach. Dajjal will ask him: 'Don't you believe in me?' He will say: 'You are the false Messiah.' He will then give his order to have him sawn with a saw into two from the parting of his hair up to his legs. After that Dajjal will walk between the two halves and will say to him: 'Stand up'"," and he will stand on his feet. He will then say to him: 'Don't you believe in me?' The person will say: 'It has added to my insight that you are Dajjal'. He will add: 'O people! He will not be able to behave with anyone amongst people in such a manner after me.' Dajjal will try to kill him. The space between his neck and collarbone will turn into copper and he will find no way to kill him. So he will catch hold of him by his hand and feet and throw him into (what appears to be the fire). The people will think that he has been thrown into the fire whereas he will be thrown into Jannah.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) added"," \""He will be the most eminent amongst the people with regard to martyrdom near the Rubb of the worlds.\"" [Muslim]"""
"1816","No one asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) more about Dajjal than I asked him. He said to me, \He will not harm you.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," it is reported that he will have with him a mountain of bread and a river full of water.\"" Thereupon he said"," \""He (Dajjal) is far too worthless and insignificant near Allah (to let him deceive the believers).\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1817","And on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is no prophet who does not warn his nation about the one-eyed liar. However, he is one-eyed, and your Lord, the Almighty and Majestic, is not one-eyed. It is written between his eyes: ‘Kafir’” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1818","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Let me tell you something about Dajjal (the Antichrist) which no Prophet had told his people. He is blind (in one eye) and will bring with him something like Jannah and Hell; but what he calls Jannah will be in fact Hell.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1819","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned the Antichrist among the people, and said: “Allah is not one-eyed, but the Antichrist is blind in his right eye, as if his eye was a floating grape” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1820","The Messenger of Allah(ﷺ) said, \The Last Hour will not come until the Muslims fight against the Jews"," until a Jew will hide himself behind a stone or a tree"," and the stone or the tree will say: 'O Muslim"," there is a Jew behind me. Come and kill him","' but Al-Gharqad tree will not say so"," for it is the tree of the Jews.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1821","And on his authority, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, this world will not pass until a man passes by a grave, wallows over it, and says: I wish I were in the place of the owner of this grave, and he has no religion, and he has nothing but affliction” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1822","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \The Hour will not come to pass before the River Euphrates dries up to unveil the mountain of gold"," for which people will fight. Ninety-nine out of one hundred will die (in the fighting) and every man amongst them will say: 'Perhaps I may be the only one to remain alive.\""' Another narration is: \""The time is near when the River Euphrates will dry up to unveil a treasure of gold. Whosoever may be alive at that time"," should not take anything of it.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"""
"1823","On his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “They will leave Medina as good as it was, and only the Awafi will cover it - he means: the Awafi of wild beasts and birds, and the last to be gathered are two shepherds from Muzainah who want to enter Medina, crowing at their sheep and finding them beasts, until when they reach Thaniyat Al-Wada’ they fall on their faces” (Agreed upon). On him).."
"1824","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “There will be a caliph [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. Your caliphs at the end of time will amass wealth but will not count it” [Muslim]."
"1825","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “A time will come upon the people in which a man will go around giving alms of gold, but he will not find anyone to take it from him, and he will see one man followed by forty women, who will find comfort in him due to the scarcity of men and the abundance of women” [Muslim]."
"1826","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “A man bought a property from another man, and the one who bought the property found in his property a jar with gold in it, and the one who bought the property said to him, ‘Take your gold’: I only bought the land from you, and I did not buy the gold. And the one who had the land said: I sold you the land and what is in it, so they took the case to a man, and the one to whom they were brought to court said: Do you have a child? One of them said: I have a boy, and he said: The other: I have a slave girl. He said: Marry the boy to the slave girl and they will spend on themselves from it and give in charity. (Agreed upon)"
"1827","And on his authority, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “There were two women with their sons. The wolf came and took the son of one of them, and she said to her companion: He only took your son. The other said: He only took your son. So they brought them to Dawud (ﷺ) and he ruled for the eldest. So they went out to Sulaiman bin Dawud (ﷺ) and they told him, and he said: Bring me a knife and cut the child between them. The younger woman said: Do not do that, may Allah have mercy on you. He is her son. So he (Sulaiman) ruled in her favor, i.e., the younger one.” (Agreed upon)"
"1828","On the authority of Muradas Al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: He said to the Prophet (ﷺ): “The righteous will go first and foremost, and scum will remain like the scum of barley or dates. Allah does not care about them.” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1829","Jibril (Gabriel) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and asked him: \How do you estimate among you those who participated in the battle of Badr?\"" He replied"," \""They were the best of Muslims\"" (or he may have said something similar to that). Jibril said: \""The same is the case with the angels who were at Badr.\"" [Al- Bukhari] ."""
"1830","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \If Allah afflicts punishment upon a nation"," it befalls the whole population indiscriminately and then they will be resurrected and judged according to their deeds.\"" [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1831","And on the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: There was a trunk to which the Prophet (ﷺ) would stand, meaning during the sermon. When the pulpit was set up, we heard the trunk like the voice of a she-ass until the Prophet (ﷺ) came down and put his hand on it, and it calmed down. And in a narration: When it was Friday, the Prophet (ﷺ) sat on the pulpit, and the palm tree by which he was delivering the sermon shouted until it almost split. She snorted. And in a narration: She shouted like a boy, so the Prophet (ﷺ) descended until he took her and hugged her to him, and she began to moan the moans of the boy being silenced until she calmed down. He said: “She cried at the remembrance she was hearing” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1832","On the authority of Abu Tha’labah al-Khushni Jurthum ibn Nashir, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “Allah Almighty has imposed obligations, so do not neglect them. He has set limits, so do not transgress them. He has forbidden things, so do not violate them. He has remained silent about certain things out of mercy for you, not out of forgetfulness, so do not search for them.” A good hadith. Narrated by Al-Daraqutni and others."
"1833","We accompanied the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in seven expeditions, and we ate locusts. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"1834","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “A believer is not stung from a hole twice” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1835","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There are three to whom Allah will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He look at them, nor will He purify them, and they will have a painful punishment: A man who has surplus water in the desert and withholds it from a traveler, A man who sold an item to another after the afternoon, and he swore by Allah to take it for such-and-such, but he believed him even though he was otherwise, and a man who gives allegiance to an imam only for worldly gain.” For this world, if he gives him of it, he will fulfill it, and if he does not give him of it, he will not fulfill it.” (Agreed upon)"
"1836","On the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “There are forty between the two blasts.” They said: O Abu Hurairah, forty days? He said: I do not specify it. They said: Forty years? He said: I do not specify it. They said: Forty months? He said: I do not specify it. And everything of man will be destroyed except for his tailbone. From it the entire creation is recreated. Then Allah sends down water from the sky. And they will grow as plants grow.” (Agreed upon)"
"1837","Once the Prophet (ﷺ) was speaking to us when, a bedouin came and asked him: \When will the Last Day be?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) continued his talk. Some of those present thought that he had heard him but disliked what he said and the other said that he had not hear him. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) concluded his speech he asked"," \""Where is the one who inquired about the Last Day?\"" The man replied: \""Here I am.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) replied"," \""When the practice of honouring a trust is lost"," expect the Last Day.\"" He asked: \""How could it be lost?\"" He replied"," \""When the government is entrusted to the undeserving people"," then wait for the Last Day.\"" [Al- Bukhari] ."""
"1838","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “They pray for you, and if they are correct, then it is yours, and if they make a mistake, then it is for you and against them” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1839","And on his authority, may Allah be pleased with him: {You are the best nation raised for mankind} He said: The best people for the people are those who bring others in chains around their necks until they enter Islam. Narrated by: Al-Bukhari."
"1840","On his authority, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Allah Almighty is astonished at a people who enter Paradise in chains” [Al-Bukhari]. It means: They are captured and tied, then they embrace Islam and they enter Paradise."
"1841","On the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “The most beloved of the countries to Allah are their mosques, and the most hated of the countries to Allah are their markets” [Muslim]."
"1842","And on the authority of Salman Al-Farsi, may Allah be pleased with him, in his saying: If you can, do not be the first to enter the market, nor the last to leave it, for it is the battle of Satan, and in it he will set up his banner. [Narrated by Muslim like this]. And Al-Barqani narrated it in his Sahih on the authority of Salman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not be the first to enter the market, nor the last to leave it, for therein is the spawn of Satan.” And a chick."
"1843","On the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sarjis, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): O Messenger of Allah, may Allah forgive you. He said: “And for you.” Asim said: So I said to him: 'Do you seek forgiveness for him, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?' He said: 'Yes, and for you.' Then he recited this verse: “And ask forgiveness for your sin. And for the believing men and believing women} [Muhammad: 19]. [Muslim]."
"1844","On the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “One of the things people realized from the words of the first prophecy was: If you are not ashamed, then do whatever you want” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1845","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “The first matter to be judged among the people on the Day of Resurrection will be bloodshed” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1846","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Angels were created from light"," jinns were created from a smokeless flame of fire"," and 'Adam was created from that which you have been told (i.e."," sounding clay like the clay of pottery).\"" [Muslim] ."""
"1847","On her authority, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: “The character of the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) was the Qur’an” [Narrated by Muslim as part of a long hadith]."
"1848","On her authority, she said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him.” So I said: O Messenger of Allah, the hatred of death? We all hate death! He said: “It is not so, but if the believer is given the good news of Allah’s mercy, satisfaction, and Paradise, he loves meeting Allah, so Allah loves meeting him, and the disbeliever when he is given the good news of Allah’s torment and displeasure, he hates meeting Allah, and Allah hated meeting him.” [Muslim]."
"1849","I came to visit the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was in the state of I'tikaf [(seclusion) in the mosque during the last ten days of Ramadan]. After having talked to him, I got up to return. The Prophet (ﷺ) also got up with me and accompanied me a part of the way. At that moment two Ansari man passed by. When they saw him they quickened their pace. The Prophet (ﷺ) said to them, \Do not hurry. She is Safiyyah"," daughter of Huyai"," my wife.\"" They said: \""Subhan Allah (Allah is free from imperfection)! O Messenger of Allah! (You are far away from any suspicion).\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""Satan circulates in a person like blood (in the blood streams). I apprehended lest Satan should drop some evil thoughts in your minds.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1850","On the authority of Abu al-Fadl al-Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the day of Hunayn, and Abu Sufyan bin al-Harith bin Abdul Muttalib joined the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and we did not separate from him while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was riding on a white mule of his. When the Muslims and polytheists met, the Muslims turned away, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) began to run with his mule before the infidels. While I was holding the bridle of the mule of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) I was trying to prevent it from speeding up while Abu Sufyan was holding the stirrup of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) “Abbas, call the owners of the brown ones.” Al-Abbas said, and he was a man of good reputation, so I said at the top of my voice: Where are the owners of the brown ones? By Allah, it was as if their kindness when they heard my voice was the kindness of cows to their young. They said: Oh Labayk, oh Labayk, so they and the infidels fought, and the call was among the Ansar saying: O people of Ansar, oh people of Ansar. Then the call was limited to Banu Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was on his mule, looked at their fighting and said: “This is when the battle became heated.” Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took pebbles and threw them at their faces. The infidels, then he said: “They are defeated, by the Lord of Muhammad.” So I went to look and saw the fighting as it was as I saw it. By Allah, he was only throwing his pebbles at them, so I continued to see their strength scattered and their ranks in full retreat. [Muslim]. And his saying: “He defined them” is with the neglected H: that is, with arrows."
"1851","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O people, Allah is good and accepts only that which is good, and Allah has commanded the believers as He commanded the messengers to do, so Allah Almighty said: {O you messengers, eat of the good and know what is good}, and Allah Almighty said: {O you who have believed, eat of the good things which We have provided for you.} Then he mentioned a man who had been traveling for a long time, disheveled and dusty, extending his hands to the sky: “O Lord, O Lord, and his food is forbidden, his drink is forbidden, his clothing is forbidden, and he was fed with forbidden food. How can he be answered?” [Muslim]."
"1852","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \There are three (types of) people whom Allah will neither speak to on the Day of Resurrection nor will He purify them (i.e."," from their sins)"," nor will look upon them; and they will have a painful chastisement. These are: An old man who commits fornication; a king who is a great liar and a poor man who is proud.\"" [Muslim]"""
"1853","On his authority, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Sihan, Jihan, the Euphrates, and the Nile are all of the rivers of Paradise” [Muslim]."
"1854","On his authority, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took my hand and said: “Allah created the soil on Saturday, and created the mountains in it on Sunday, and created the trees on Monday, and created the hated thing on Tuesday, and created light on Wednesday, and spread the animals in it on Thursday, and created Adam (ﷺ) after the afternoon of Friday at the end of creation in the last hour of the day between afternoon and night” [Muslim]."
"1855","On the authority of Abu Suleiman Khalid bin Al-Walid, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: “Nine swords were cut off from my hand on the day of his death, and all that remained in my hand was a Yemeni plate” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1856","I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, \When a judge utilizes his skill of judgement and comes to a right decision"," he will have a double reward"," but when he uses his judgement and commits a mistake"," he will have a single reward.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"""
"1857","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, \Fever comes from the vehement raging of Hell"," so cool it with water.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1858","On the authority of her, may Allah be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Whoever dies and is obligated to fast, his guardian will fast on his behalf” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1859","And on the authority of Auf bin Malik bin Al-Tufayl that Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, narrated that Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, may Allah be pleased with them both, said in a sale or tender that Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: By Allah, you will stop Aisha, or I will quarantine her. She said: Did he say this? They said: Yes, she said: It is for Allah. I have vowed never to speak to Ibn Al-Zubayr, so Ibn Al-Zubayr sought intercession for her when the migration took a long time, and she said: No, by Allah. I will never intercede for him, nor will I break my vow. So when Ibn al-Zubayr had gone on for a long time, Al-Miswar spoke to Ibn Makhramah and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth and said to them: I adjure you by Allah when you introduced me to Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, for it is not permissible for her to vow my flock. So al-Miswar and Abd al-Rahman approached him until they sought permission from Aisha, and they said: May the peace, mercy, and blessings of Allah be upon you. Shall we enter? She said. Aisha: Come in. They said: All of us? She said: Yes, come in, all of you, and you do not know that Ibn al-Zubayr is with them. When they entered, Ibn al-Zubayr entered the veil, and he embraced Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, and began to appeal to her and cry. Al-Maswar and Abd al-Rahman began to appeal to her, except that she spoke to him and she accepted from him, and they said: The Prophet (ﷺ) forbade what she had learned about emigration, and it is not permissible to do so. Muslim had the right to abandon his brother for more than three nights, but when they made a lot of reminding and harassing Aisha, she started remembering them and crying, and saying: I made a vow and the vow was severe. They did not stop until she spoke to Ibn al-Zubayr, and as a result of her vow she freed forty slaves. After that, she would remember her vow and cry until her tears soaked her veil. [Al-Bukhari]."
"1860","And on the authority of Uqba bin Amer, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out to the dead of Uhud and prayed over them after eight years like a farewell to the living and the dead. Then he went up to the pulpit and said: I am in your hands and I am a witness over you, and your appointment is the Basin, and I look at it from this position of mine, and I am not afraid that you will associate others with this world, but I fear that you will compete with this world. Her look at the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration: “But I fear for you in this world that you will compete in it and fight each other and be destroyed as those who were before you perished.” Uqba said: The last thing I saw of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was on the pulpit. And in a narration he said: “I am a supremacist for you and I am a witness against you.” By Allah, I look at my basin now, and I have been given the keys to the treasures of the earth, or the keys to the earth, and by Allah I do not fear that you will associate others with others after me, but I fear that you will compete in it.” What is meant by praying for the dead of Uhud is to pray for them, not the known prayer"
"1861","On the authority of Abu Zaid Amr bin Akhtab Al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led us in the dawn prayer, and ascended the pulpit, so he preached to us until noon arrived, so he descended and prayed, then ascended the pulpit until afternoon prayer, then he descended and prayed, then ascended the pulpit until the sun set, so he told us what was going to happen, and taught us what preserves us. [Muslim]"
"1862","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, \He who vows to obey Allah"," should obey Him. But he who vows to disobey Allah"," should not disobey Him.\"" [Al- Bukhari] ."""
"1863","-On the authority of Umm Sharik, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered her to kill the lizards and said: “It (the lizard) used to blow on Abraham” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1864","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \He who kills a chameleon at the first blow"," such and such number of good deeds will be awarded to him; whoever kills it at the second blow"," such and such number of merits will be recorded for him. And if he kills it at the third blow"," he will get such and such merits.\"" Another narration is: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""If anyone kills a chameleon with the first blow"," a hundred good deeds will be recorded for him; less than that will be recorded for him if he kills it at the second blow"," and still less rewards will be recorded for him if he kills it at the third blow.\"" [Muslim] . The scholars of language said: 'Al-Wazagh (the lizard) is the large (type) of the sam (a lizard species) that is leprous.'"""
"1865","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A man said: ‘Should I give charity?’ So he went out with his charity and placed it in the hand of a thief. They started talking: Give charity to a thief! So he went out with his charity and put it in the hands of a rich man. They started talking! Tonight you gave charity to a rich man. He said: Oh Allah, praise be to you for a thief, for an adulterer, and for a rich man! So he came and was told: As for your charity for a thief, perhaps he will refrain from stealing. As for the adulteress, perhaps she will refrain from her adultery. As for the rich man, Perhaps he will consider it and spend from what Allah has given him.” [Al-Bukhari])."
"1866","On his authority, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in an invitation, and he raised his arm to him, and he liked it, so he bit off a piece of it and said: I am the master of people on the Day of Resurrection. Do you know who that is? Allah gathers the first and the last in one level, so the observer sees them, and the one who invites hears them, and they come close to the sun, so the people reach such anguish and anguish that they cannot bear it, so the people say: Don’t you see? What are you in and what has reached you? Do you not look for someone to intercede for you with your Lord? Then some people say to one another: Your father is Adam, and they come to him and say: O Adam, you are the father of mankind. Allah created you with His hand, and breathed into you His spirit, and commanded the angels, so they prostrated to you and made you dwell in Paradise. Will you not intercede for us with your Lord? Do you not see what we are in, and what we have reached? Then he said: Indeed, my Lord is angry today with an anger such as He has never been angry with before, and He will never be angry with such anger again., and he forbade me from the tree, so I disobeyed, myself, myself, myself, go to someone else, go to Noah, and they come to Noah and say: O Noah, you are the first of the messengers to the people of the earth, and Allah has called you a grateful servant. Do you not see what we are in? Do you not see what we have reached? Will you not intercede for us with your Lord? Then he says: Indeed, my Lord is angry today with an anger that He has never been angry with before. He will never be angry like him after him, and I have had a supplication that I made upon my people. Myself, myself, myself. Go to someone else. Go to Abraham. So they come to Abraham and say: O Abraham, you are the prophet of Allah and his friend among the people of the earth. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what we are in? So he says to them: My Lord is angry today with an anger that he has never been angry like before, and he will never be angry like him after him. And I have told three lies. Myself, myself, myself. Go to Other than me, go to Moses. They come to Moses and say: O Moses, you are the Messenger of Allah. Allah has favored you with His messages and His words to the people. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what we are in? So he says: My Lord has become angry today with an anger that He has never been angry like before, and He will never be angry like Him after Him. Indeed, I have killed a soul that I was not commanded to kill. Myself, Myself, Myself. Go to someone else. Go to Jesus. So they come. Jesus, and they say: O Jesus, you are the Messenger of Allah, and His word He delivered to Mary and a spirit from Him, and you spoke to the people in the cradle. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what we are in? Then Jesus says: My Lord is angry today with an anger that He has never been angry like before, and He will never be angry like Him after Him, and He has not mentioned a sin. My soul, my soul, my soul, go to others, go to Muhammad (ﷺ). And in a narration: “So they come to me and say: O Muhammad, you are the Messenger of Allah and the Seal of the Prophets, and your past and future sins have been forgiven. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see what we are in? So I go and come under the Throne, and I fall prostrating to my Lord. Then Allah will bestow upon me one of His praises, and praise Him in a way that has never been bestowed upon anyone before me. Then it will be said: O Muhammad, raise your head, ask. You grant him, and I intercede and you will intercede, so I raise my head and say, “My nation, O Lord, my nation, O Lord,” and it is said: “O Muhammad, bring in from your nation those for whom there is no reckoning through the right door of the gates of Paradise, and they will be partners with people in other gates.” Then he said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, the distance between the two gates of Paradise is like the distance between Mecca and Hijra, or like the distance between Mecca and Busra” (Agreed upon). On him).."
"1867","Ibrahim (ﷺ) brought his wife and her son Isma'il (ﷺ) while she was suckling him, to a place near the Ka'bah under a tree on the spot of Zamzam, at the highest place in the mosque. In those days, there was no human being in Makkah, nor was there any water. So he made them sit over there and placed near them a leather bag containing some dates, and a small water-skin containing some water, and set out homeward. Isma'il's mother followed him saying: \O Ibrahim! Where are you going"," leaving us in this valley where there is no person whose company we may enjoy"," nor is there anything (to enjoy)?\"" She repeated that to him many times"," but he did not look back at her. Then she asked him: \""Has Allah commanded you to do so?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" She said: \""Then He will not neglect us.\"" She returned while Ibrahim proceeded onwards. Having reached the Thaniya"," where they could see him"," he faced Ka'bah"," raised his both hands and supplicated: \""O our Rubb! I have made some of my offspring to dwell in an uncultivable valley by Your Sacred House (the Ka'bah at Makkah) in order"," O our Rubb"," that they may perform As-Salat (Iqamat-as-Salat). So fill some hearts among men with love towards them"," and (O Allah) provide them with fruits so that they may give thanks.\"" (14:37). Isma'il's mother went on suckling Isma'il and drinking from the water which she had. When the water in the water-skin had all been used up"," she became thirsty and her child also became thirsty. She started looking at Isma'il"," tossing in agony. She left him"," for she could not endure looking at him"," and found that the mountain of As-Safa was the nearest mountain to her on that land. She stood on it and started looking at the valley keenly so that she might see somebody"," but she could not see anybody. Then she descended from As-Safa"," and when she reached the valley"," she tucked up her robe and ran in the valley like a person in distress and trouble till she crossed the valley and reached Al-Marwah mountain where she stood and started looking"," expecting to see somebody"," but she could not see anybody. She repeated that (running between As-Safa and Al-Marwah) seven times.\"" Ibn 'Abbas further related: The Prophet (ﷺ) said"," \""This is the source of the tradition of the Sa'y - i.e."," the going of people between the two mountains. When she reached Al-Marwah (for the last time)"," she heard a voice and she exclaimed: 'Shshs!' (Silencing herself) and listened attentively. She heard the voice again and said: 'O (whoever you may be) You have made me hear your voice; have you any succour for me?' And behold! She saw an angel at the place of Zamzam"," digging the earth with his heel (or with his wing)"," till water flowed out from that place. She started to make something like of a basin around it"," using her hands in this way and began to fill her water- skin with water with her hands"," and the water was flowing out until she had scooped some of it.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) further said"," \""May Allah bestow mercy on Isma'il's mother! Had she let the Zamzam flow without trying to control it (or had she not scooped in that water) while filling her water-skin"," Zamzam would have been a stream flowing on the surface of the earth.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) further added"," \""Then she drank (water) and suckled her child. The angel said to her: 'Do not be afraid of being neglected"," for this is the site on which the House of Allah will be built by this boy and his father"," and Allah will never let neglected His people.' The House of Allah (the Ka'bah) at that time was on a high place resembling a hillock"," and when torrents came"," they flowed to its right and left. She continued living in that way till some people from the tribe of Jurhum passed by her and her child. As they were coming from through the way of Kada'"," in the lower part of Makkah where they saw a bird that had a habit of flying around water and not leaving it. They said: 'This bird must be flying over water"," though we know that there is no water in this valley.' They sent one or two messengers who discovered the source of water"," and returned to inform them of the water. So"," they all came towards the water.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) added"," \""Isma'il's mother was sitting near the water. They asked her: 'Do you allow us to stay with you?' She replied: 'Yes"," but you will have no right to possess the water.' They agreed to that.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) further said"," \""Isma'il's mother was pleased with the whole situation as she used to love the company of the people. So"," they settled there"," and later on they sent for their families who came and settled with them. The child (i.e."," Isma'il) grew up and learnt Arabic from them (his virtues) caused them to love and admire him as he grew up"," and when he reached the age of puberty"," they gave him one of their daughters in marriage. After Isma'il's mother had died"," Ibrahim came after Isma'il's marriage in order to see his family that he had left before"," but he did not find Isma'il there. When he asked Isma'il's wife about him"," she replied: 'He has gone in search of our livelihood.' Then he asked her about their way of living and their condition"," and she replied complaining to him: 'We are living in hardship"," misery and destitution.' He said: 'When your husband returns"," convey my salutations to him and tell him to change the threshold of the door of his house.' When Isma'il came"," he seemed to have perceived something unusual. He asked his wife: 'Did anyone visit you?' She replied: 'Yes"," an old man of such and such description came and asked me about you and I informed him"," and he asked about our state of living"," and"," I told him that we were living in hardship and poverty.' Thereupon Isma'il said: 'Did he advise you anything?' She replied: 'Yes"," he told me to convey his salutations to you and to change the threshold of your door.' Isma'il said: 'That was my father"," and he has ordered me to divorce you. Go back to your family.' So Isma'il divorced her and married another woman from amongst them (Jurhum). Then Ibrahim stayed away from them for a period as long as Allah wished"," and called on them again but did not find Isma'il. So he came to Isma'il's wife and asked her about him. She said: 'He has gone in search of our livelihood.' Ibrahim asked her about their sustenance and living: 'How are you getting on?' She replied: 'We are prosperous and well off.' Then she praised Allah"," the Exalted. Ibrahim asked: 'What kind of food do you eat?' She said: 'Meat.' He said: 'What do you drink?' She said: 'Water.' He said"," 'O Allah! Bless their meat and water!\""' The Prophet (ﷺ) added"," \""At that time they did not have grain"," and if they had grain"," he would have also invoked Allah to bless it.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) further said"," \""If somebody has only these two things as his sustenance"," his health and disposition will be badly affected because these things do not suit him unless he lives in Makkah.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) added"," \""Then Ibrahim said to Isma'il's wife"," 'When your husband comes"," give my regards to him and tell him that he should keep firm the threshold of his door.' When Isma'il came back"," he asked his wife: 'Did anyone call on you?' She replied: 'Yes"," a good looking old man came to me.' She praised him and added: 'He asked about you"," and I informed him"," and he asked about our livelihood and I told him that we were in good condition.' Isma'il asked her: 'Did he give you a piece of advice?' She said: 'Yes"," he told me to convey his regards to you and ordered that you should keep firm the threshold of your door.' On that Isma'il said: 'He was my father and you are the threshold of the door. He has ordered me to keep you with me.' Then Ibrahim stayed away from them for a period as long as Allah wished and called on them afterwards. He saw Isma'il under a tree near Zamzam"," sharpening his arrows. When he saw Ibrahim"," he rose up to welcome him"," and they greeted each other as a father does with his son or a son does with his father. Ibrahim said: 'O Isma'il! Allah has given me an order.' Isma'il said: 'Do what your Rubb has commanded you to do.' Ibrahim asked: 'Will you help me?' Isma'il said: 'I will help you.' Ibrahim said: 'Allah has ordered me to build a house here"," pointing to a hillock higher than the land surrounding it.\""' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) added"," \""Then they raised the foundations of the House (i.e."," Ka'bah). Isma'il brought the stones and Ibrahim was building (the house). When the walls became high"," Isma'il brought stone and placed it for Ibrahim who stood over it and carried on building the House"," while Isma'il was handing over the stones to him"," both of them prayed: 'O our Rubb! Accept this service from us! Verily"," You are the All- Hearer and the All-Knower.\""' [Al-Bukhari] . There are some more narrations about this incident"," some adding details and some with minor variations in the wordings."""
"1868","On the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Truffles are from manna, and their water is a cure for the eyes” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
